        <item>
            <title>0.81</title>
            <pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 09:39:04 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1791106320</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.81</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; padding: 12px; }
  h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 14px; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 12px; }
  ul { margin: 4px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin: 2px 0; }
</style>
<h3>What's New</h3>
<h2>New Features</h2>
<ul>
<li>Agents can now build custom pane types. Each one is a small HTML/JS app in its own folder under ~/Library/Application Support/Addy/Panes/&lt;kind&gt;/, with a pane.json manifest. It renders as a native pane that hot-reloads when its files change.</li>
<li>Custom panes get a window.addy bridge. It covers project file read/write/list, shell commands (addy.run), per-project storage, opening URLs in Addy&#x27;s browser, and theme variables that follow the active theme.</li>
<li>Installed custom panes appear in the pane launcher. A new &quot;New Pane Type…&quot; action asks what you want and starts an agent that builds it.</li>
<li>Two new agent tools, addy_list_pane_types and addy_open_custom_pane, let agents list installed pane types, read the authoring guide, and open or reload a custom pane. They can then check its text and JavaScript errors with addy_read_pane.</li>
<li>Browser panes now show JavaScript alert, confirm and prompt dialogs inline in the pane instead of silently ignoring them.</li>
<li>Browser downloads now save straight to ~/Downloads without overwriting existing files. A toast confirms each download with a &quot;Show in Finder&quot; action, or reports the failure.</li>
<li>Browser panes now capture console.log, warn, error and info output, plus uncaught errors and rejections. A pane keeps up to 2,000 entries.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Improvements</h2>
<ul>
<li>When an agent&#x27;s browser action triggers a page dialog, it is answered automatically (OK for alerts, Cancel otherwise) so the agent isn&#x27;t blocked. The agent sees a console warning describing what happened.</li>
<li>File pickers in browser panes only open for you, never during agent-driven actions.</li>
<li>Hidden browser panes now pause media playback right away. They unload their page after 5 minutes, or immediately under memory pressure, and restore it when you return.</li>
<li>Custom panes persist across layouts and restarts. Their data is stored outside the pane folder, so saving it doesn&#x27;t trigger a reload.</li>
<li>Custom pane links to web pages open in Addy&#x27;s browser pane. Pages from the web can&#x27;t call the bridge.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Bug Fixes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Clicking a download link in the browser pane no longer replaces the page with an error page.</li>
<li>Reloading or navigating a hidden browser pane no longer gets confused by the &quot;paused while hidden&quot; placeholder. Its title and URL are no longer overwritten.</li>
<li>Fixed the note shown when a page opens in a project you aren&#x27;t viewing. It now correctly says browser tools can&#x27;t reach the page until you switch to that project.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
